{
  "id": "V14",
  "title": "FTAO — APA T555 two-opening benchmark",
  "intent": "A 19.5 ft FTAO wall with two windows reproduces the APA T555 two-opening example through the whole calculator (level load → share → FTAO engine). The statics of the force-transfer method must match the published Figure 4 values: chord force H, unit shear above / below the openings, pier and corner-zone unit shears, strap force F_max and the corner forces.",
  "covers": [
    "FTAO method (APA T555 / Diekmann)",
    "Published benchmark (APA T555 Figure 4)",
    "Segmented vs FTAO: openings only on FTAO walls"
  ],
  "handCalc": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "Geometry (T555): piers 4 / 4 / 3.5 ft, openings 6 / 2 ft → L = 19.5 ft; h = 8 ft, h_a = 1.33, h_o = 2.67, h_b = 4 ft. In the tool: openings at offset 4 ft (width 6) and 14 ft (width 2), sill 4 ft, head 6.67 ft."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "Loads: T555 uses V_ASD = 3750 lb. With seismic 0.7ρE and ρ = 1 the level load is V = 3750 / 0.7 = 5357.14 lb (entered as 5.36 k, one wall takes all of it)."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "Chord force H = V·h / L = 3750 × 8 / 19.5 = 1538.46 lb (published 1,538 lb; no dead load in the FTAO statics)."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "Unit shear above and below the openings v_a = v_b = H / (h_a + h_b) = 1538.46 / (1.33 + 4) = 288.46 plf (published 288 plf)."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "Pier unit shears (published): pier 1 / 2 / 3 = 337 / 388 / 244 plf; corner-zone unit shears v_c = 120 / 95 / 167 plf."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "Strap force F_max (published) = 865 lb; corner forces: opening 1 left / right = 865 / 865 lb, opening 2 left / right = 308 / 269 lb."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "text": "Anchorage along the wall = V / L = 3750 / 19.5 = 192.31 plf."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "text": "Line checks: base shear and moment of the one wall = the level load → G1–G12 pass."
    },
    {
      "step": 9,
      "text": "FTAO deflection at 1.0E (APA T555 method: Eq. 4.3-1 for each pier in each direction, averaged; pinned design 4\" o.c. plywood G_a = 20, HDUE3 δ 0.127 in at 3,790 lb, all pier edges (2)2x4 A = 10.5 in²; the published 0.335 in uses the example’s own components, so it is not this case’s value). V = 5357.14 lb, H = V·h/L = 2197.80 lb. Pier 1 L: v = 5357.14/19.5 × (L_1 + T_1) / L_1 = 5357.14/19.5 × (4 + 3.000)/4 = 480.77 plf, h = 8 → 0.0276 + 0.1923 + 8 × (0.1289 + Δ_c 0.0092 [r = 0.335])/4 = 0.4960; Pier 1 R: v = 5357.14/19.5 × (L_1 + T_1) / L_1 = 5357.14/19.5 × (4 + 3.000)/4 = 480.77 plf, h = 4 → 0.0034 + 0.0962 + 4 × (0.0644)/4 = 0.1640; Pier 2 L: v = 5357.14/19.5 × (L_2 + T_2) / L_2 = 5357.14/19.5 × (4 + 4.067)/4 = 554.03 plf, h = 4 → 0.0040 + 0.1108 + 4 × (0.0743)/4 = 0.1890; Pier 2 R: v = 5357.14/19.5 × (L_2 + T_2) / L_2 = 5357.14/19.5 × (4 + 4.067)/4 = 554.03 plf, h = 4 → 0.0040 + 0.1108 + 4 × (0.0743)/4 = 0.1890; Pier 3 L: v = 5357.14/19.5 × (L_3 + T_3) / L_3 = 5357.14/19.5 × (3.5 + 0.933)/3.5 = 347.99 plf, h = 4 → 0.0029 + 0.0696 + 4 × (0.0466)/3.5 = 0.1258; Pier 3 R: v = 5357.14/19.5 × (L_3 + T_3) / L_3 = 5357.14/19.5 × (3.5 + 0.933)/3.5 = 347.99 plf, h = 8 → 0.0228 + 0.1392 + 8 × (0.0933 + Δ_c 0.0092 [r = 0.335])/3.5 = 0.3962 → Δ = average of the 6 cases = 0.2600 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 10,
      "text": "Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-14 0.2600 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.2600 / 1.0 = 1.040 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 8 × 12 = 1.920 in → OK."
    }
  ],
